WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
French prisons have never
held so many people.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:08.840
On 1 October 2026: 90,937.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.000
A record. One year earlier,

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.690
the figure was 84,862.

5
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.560
There are far fewer places than prisoners.

6
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.040
Some sleep on mattresses on the floor.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.710
Critics call prison «l'école du crime».

8
00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.030
Supporters say «la prison
protège la société».

9
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.400
So does prison actually work,

10
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.760
or are there better ways to punish?

11
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.460
In this mission, you'll climb Mission D1,

12
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.660
from «une contravention» to «un crime»,

13
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.500
and follow a case from arrest to release.

14
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.840
Then you'll line up the
alternatives in Mission D2,

15
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:45.100
from a fine to an electronic tag,

16
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.110
and decide which ones work.

17
00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:51.080
Your mission: weigh the evidence
and decide whether prison works,

18
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.610
or what should replace it.
